**Given:**

25 paise, 10 paise and 5 paise coins are in the ratio of 1 : 2 : 3 in a bag. The total value of money is Rs. 180

**Concept Used:**

Concept of ratio and proportion

**Calculation:**

The ratio of 25 paise, 10 paise and 5 paise is 1 : 2 : 3

Let, the number of coins are y, 2y and 3y respectively

Total number of money is Rs. 180 = 180 × 100

⇒ 18000 paise

Accordingly,

(25 × y) + (10 × 2y) + (5 × 3y) = 18000

⇒ 25y + 20y + 15y = 18000

⇒ 60y = 18000

⇒ y = 300

Number of 10 paise coins is 2 × 300 = 600

**∴ There will be 600 coins of 10 paise**

.responsive-table {
 width: 100%;
 max-width: 600px;
 margin: 20px auto;
 border-collapse: collapse;
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 text-align: center;
 }
 .responsive-table thead tr {
 background-color: rgb(0, 195, 182);
 color: black;
 }
 .responsive-table th, .responsive-table td {
 padding: 12px 8px;
 border: 1px solid #ddd;
 white-space: normal; /* Allow wrapping */
 }
 @media (max-width: 600px) {
 .responsive-table thead {
 display: table-header-group; /* Keep header visible */
 background-color: rgb(74, 206, 222);
 color: black;
 }
 .responsive-table tbody, .responsive-table tr, .responsive-table td {
 display: block;
 width: 100%;
 }
 .responsive-table tr {
 margin-bottom: 15px;
 border-bottom: 2px solid rgb(74, 206, 222);
 }
 .responsive-table td {
 text-align: right;
 padding-left: 50%;
 position: relative;
 border: none;
 border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
 white-space: normal; /* Allow wrapping */
 }
 .responsive-table td::before {
 content: attr(data-label);
 position: absolute;
 left: 10px;
 top: 12px;
 font-weight: bold;
 text-align: left;
 white-space: normal; /* Allow wrapping */
 }
 }
